{"id":"f2a8182491507d2f2234596bd54e86c5d4d1fcfd","axis":"silent","repo":"hibernate/hibernate-orm","sha":"f2a8182491507d2f2234596bd54e86c5d4d1fcfd","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"documentation/src/main/asciidoc/userguide/chapters/locking/Locking.adoc","lines":["@@ -134,6 +134,17 @@ For a versioned entity, requesting `PESSIMISTIC_FORCE_INCREMENT` after `PESSIMIS"," Repeating `PESSIMISTIC_FORCE_INCREMENT` when that mode is already held does not cause another increment merely because the request is repeated."," Choose the required mode before relying on its increment behavior."," ","+For direct entity loading with `PESSIMISTIC_FORCE_INCREMENT` and `EXTENDED` scope, Hibernate completes supplemental collection-table locking before performing the requested version increments.","+The direct read establishes root protection; while supplemental acquisition is pending, the recorded mode is `PESSIMISTIC_WRITE`.","+Lifecycle callbacks, including `@PostLoad`, and row/tuple transformation still run during loading and may observe the original version and pending protection.","+For these executions, result-list transformation runs after acquisition and increment completion, so it observes the completed versions.","+Streams and scrolls complete the current logical result before exposing it, including results that were already managed.","+A failure on a later cursor result does not undo earlier results, and closing a cursor does not increment unconsumed results.","+","+An optimistic force increment scheduled before a pessimistic force increment remains independent: the pessimistic increment occurs before result exposure, and the scheduled optimistic increment may advance the version again before commit.","+Failed pessimistic acquisition does not cancel that previously scheduled optimistic work.","+An optimistic force-increment request made after pessimistic protection is already held retains the mode-composition behavior described above.","+"," Mode ordering and scope acquisition are separate concerns."," An `EXTENDED` pessimistic request can acquire collection-table and owned join-table locks even when the entity already holds an equal or stronger mode."," Repeating the request can be necessary after collection replacement or changes to the relevant managed state."],"additions":11,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"hibernate-core/src/main/java/org/hibernate/LockMode.java","lines":["@@ -173,6 +173,11 @@ public enum LockMode implements FindOption, RefreshOption {"," \t * {@link #PESSIMISTIC_READ} or {@link #PESSIMISTIC_WRITE} increments the"," \t * version immediately. Repeating this mode when it is already held by a"," \t * stateful session does not itself cause another increment.","+\t * <p>","+\t * Direct loads using {@link PessimisticLockScope#EXTENDED} complete","+\t * supplemental collection locking before incrementing. Loading callbacks may","+\t * observe the original version and provisional {@link #PESSIMISTIC_WRITE}","+\t * protection; the increment completes before the result is exposed."," \t *"," \t * @see LockModeType#PESSIMISTIC_FORCE_INCREMENT"," \t */"],"additions":5,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"hibernate-core/src/main/java/org/hibernate/internal/scrollable/AbstractScrollableResults.java","lines":["@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@"," import org.hibernate.sql.results.jdbc.spi.JdbcValuesSourceProcessingOptions;"," import org.hibernate.sql.results.jdbc.spi.JdbcValuesSourceProcessingState;"," import org.hibernate.sql.results.spi.RowReader;","+import org.hibernate.sql.exec.internal.lock.DirectLockingCompletion;"," "," /**","  * Base implementation of the ScrollableResults interface intended for sharing between","@@ -78,6 +79,20 @@ protected void afterScrollOperation() {"," \t\tgetPersistenceContext().afterScrollOperation();"," \t}"," ","+\tprotected void checkLockingCompletionActive() {","+\t\tfinal var completion = DirectLockingCompletion.from( jdbcValuesSourceProcessingState.getLoadedValuesCollector() );","+\t\tif ( completion != nu